    description:
      '🔹 WHAT IS useEffect?\nuseEffect is a React Hook used to synchronize a component with external systems and perform side effects outside the rendering process.\n\n🔹 COMMON USE CASES\n📌 Fetching data from APIs\n📌 Document title updates\n📌 Setting timers & intervals\n📌 Adding/removing event listeners\n📌 Local storage synchronization & WebSocket subscriptions\n\n🔹 REAL-TIME SEARCH EXAMPLE\nUser types in search box ⬇️ Search state updates ⬇️ useEffect detects change ⬇️ API request triggers ⬇️ State updates with results ⬇️ UI renders search results\n\n🔹 COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID\n❌ Forgetting necessary dependencies in the array\n❌ Missing cleanup functions for timers/listeners\n❌ Using effects for calculations that can be derived directly during render\n\n💡 PRO TIP\nIf something can be calculated directly during rendering (e.g., const fullName = firstName + " " + lastName;), you do not need useEffect.\n\n🎯 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS\n1️⃣ What is useEffect?\n👉 A React Hook used to synchronize components with external systems and manage side effects.\n\n2️⃣ When does useEffect run?\n👉 It runs after rendering. Its execution depends on the values provided in its dependency array.\n\n3️⃣ What is a cleanup function?\n👉 A function returned by the effect that cleans up resources (timers, listeners) before the component unmounts or before re-running the effect.\n\n4️⃣ What does the dependency array do?\n👉 It tells React which reactive values the effect depends on, dictating when it should re-run.',
