      "🔹 WHY IS STYLING IMPORTANT?\nGood styling provides a professional UI, better user experience, responsive layouts, and consistent design across an application.\n\n🔹 COMMON WAYS TO STYLE REACT\n1️⃣ Standard CSS Stylesheets\n2️⃣ Inline Styles (style={{ color: 'red' }})\n3️⃣ CSS Modules\n4️⃣ CSS-in-JS (Styled Components, Emotion)\n5️⃣ Utility-first frameworks (Tailwind CSS)\n6️⃣ Component Libraries (MUI, Shadcn, Chakra UI)\n\n🔹 RESPONSIVE DESIGN & LAYOUTS\n📌 Flexbox: Ideal for one-dimensional layouts (navbars, centering content, card rows).\n📌 CSS Grid: Ideal for two-dimensional layouts (product grids, dashboards, image galleries).\n📌 Media Queries: Ensure smooth responsiveness across mobile, tablet, and desktop screens.\n\n🎯 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS\n1️⃣ How do you style React components?\n👉 Using external CSS, inline styles, CSS Modules, CSS-in-JS, Tailwind CSS, or component libraries.\n\n2️⃣ What is className?\n👉 The JSX attribute equivalent to HTML's class attribute.\n\n3️⃣ What is the difference between CSS Grid and Flexbox?\n👉 Flexbox is designed for 1D layouts (rows or columns), while CSS Grid handles 2D layouts (rows and columns simultaneously).\n\n4️⃣ How can you apply conditional styles?\n👉 Using conditional className strings (e.g., `btn ${isActive ? 'active' : ''}`), dynamic style objects, or libraries like clsx.",
